ACTUATOR is a monitoring library for Java applications that provides production-ready features to help you monitor and manage your application. It offers a variety of endpoints that expose information about the application's health, metrics, environment, and more.
PROMETHEUS is a 3rd party tool that pulls data from Actuator and scrapes metrics exposed by Spring Boot Actuator’s Prometheus endpoint and stores them in a time-series database for querying and visualization. It is exposed via the /actuator/prometheus endpoint. (default port: 9090)
GRAFANA is an open-source platform for monitoring and observability that allows you to visualize and analyze data from various sources, including Prometheus. It provides a powerful and flexible way to create dashboards and alerts based on the metrics collected by Prometheus. (default port: 3000, username: admin, password: admin)
ZIPKIN is a distributed tracing system that helps you analyze and debug microservices-based applications. Its main purpose of usage is to understand and debug how a single request flows across multiple microservices, and where time is being spent. (default port: 9411)